# Git push — wait for confirmation

- Do **not** push to origin (or any remote) unless the user explicitly asks to push after they have tested locally.
- Commits are allowed when the user asks to commit; push is a separate step.
- If the user says “commit and push”, still treat push as requiring clear go-ahead after local test — ask first if they have not confirmed the change is good.
- Never run `git push` proactively after finishing a feature.
